# ── Lead capture ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Leads must reach:  hello@californialawfirmseo.com
#                    contact@bytezeroinc.com
#
# This site is a static SPA — it cannot send email itself. It POSTs the
# submission as JSON to a relay, and the relay sends the notification.
# Set VITE_LEAD_ENDPOINT to that relay in the deploy environment
# (Replit → Secrets). Until it is set, the form shows an error and falls
# back to a mailto link — it will never silently swallow a lead.

VITE_LEAD_ENDPOINT=

# Who gets notified. Comma-separated. Sent to the relay in the payload as
# `recipients`, and used for the mailto fallback.
# Optional — defaults to the two addresses above.
VITE_LEAD_RECIPIENTS=hello@californialawfirmseo.com,contact@bytezeroinc.com


# ── Picking a relay ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Option A — n8n (you already run bytezero26.app.n8n.cloud)
#   New workflow: Webhook (POST) → Send Email.
#   Address the email to both inboxes, or read the `recipients` array
#   from the payload. Set VITE_LEAD_ENDPOINT to the production webhook URL.
#   Best option: leads can also go to a sheet/CRM in the same flow.
#
# Option B — Formspree / Web3Forms / Zapier catch hook
#   Sign up, create a form/hook, set VITE_LEAD_ENDPOINT to the URL it gives
#   you, and add the second address as a CC in that service's settings.
#   Fastest to get live; a third party holds the leads.
#
# Whichever you pick, the endpoint must accept a JSON POST and allow CORS
# from the site's origin.


# ── Payload POSTed to VITE_LEAD_ENDPOINT ──────────────────────
# {
#   "name": "John Smith",
#   "email": "john@lawfirm.com",
#   "firm": "Smith & Associates",
#   "practice": "Personal Injury",
#   "message": "...",
#   "subject": "Strategy call request — Smith & Associates",
#   "recipients": ["hello@californialawfirmseo.com", "contact@bytezeroinc.com"],
#   "source": "footer" | "contact-section",
#   "site": "ca-lawfirm-seo",
#   "submitted_at": "2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z",
#   "page_url": "https://.../ai-seo-law-firms-california",
#   "page_path": "/ai-seo-law-firms-california",
#   "referrer": "https://google.com/",
#   "utm_source": "...", "utm_medium": "...", "utm_campaign": "...",
#   "utm_term": "...", "utm_content": "...", "gclid": "..."
# }
